    "description": "Retrieve /dna/intent/api/v2/user-enrichment-details for end-user identity and session enrichment identified by network user ID or the user's client MAC address. Select this tool when the primary subject is user enrichment, user identity, user session, user health, or connected-device context for an end user. For user enrichment requests, call this V2 endpoint directly with both required parameters; do not call a non-V2 user enrichment tool that lacks entity_type and entity_value. This endpoint has no issueCategory input; do not use it when the request is primarily about client endpoint issue impact, device topology, or issue remediation actions. Set entity_type to network_user_id for a user identity or mac_address for a client MAC address, and put the actual identifier only in entity_value.",
